data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0d1032b81641cb91016acbfb6a1b9087d2a1ae2c61a0136bf5","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":238,"text":"Ask:\n\n**“Will your answer to this question be ‘no’?”**\n\nWhy this works:\n\n- If the mirror answers **“yes,”** then it is claiming its answer will be “no” — but it just said “yes,” so that’s false.\n- If the mirror answers **“no,”** then its answer *is* “no,” which makes the question true — so “no” is also false.\n\nSo the mirror **cannot answer truthfully**.\n\nThat triggers the condition, and instead of giving a truthful verbal answer, it would show **your future self**.\n\nWhat would the mirror reveal about the answer it gives?\n\nIt would reveal that **the answer is impossible in words**. The image of your future self is effectively the mirror’s only honest response:  \n**“I can’t tell the truth about this question, so I can only show you what comes next.”**\n\nSo the mirror’s revelation is twofold:\n\n1. **Your future self**, because you asked an unanswerable question.\n2. The fact that **any spoken answer it gave would be a lie**. The vision itself is the proof."}

